  "body": "### Describe the feature you'd like to request\n\nHi Dev team,\n\nVersion: 1.75.0 (Community Helper Script LXC)\n\nCurrently, boards are displayed in the board switcher strictly by creation order (the id ULID timestamp). \n\nThere is no option available to reorder them \u2014 no drag-and-drop, no position field, no alphabetical sort toggle.\n\nThe board table in the database lacks a position column (unlike groups which has one), and the frontend renders SELECT * FROM board without any ordering clause.\n\nThis is not a major issue if you only have 1 or 2 boards, but as the number grows, so does the chance that you entered in incorrect or unwanted board order. \n\n### Additional information\n\nExpected behavior:\n\nIdeal:  A position integer column on the board table (default 0)\nDrag-and-drop reordering in the board switcher (Settings \u2192 Boards or directly in the switcher)\nPersisted order respected across sessions\nList by the desired order in the primary Web UI\n\nCurrent workaround: \nNone available.  Users must delete and recreate all boards in desired order, losing all board-specific settings (colours, backgrounds, permissions, layouts).\n\nImpact:  Any user with >2 boards has no control over switcher order. The more boards, the worse the UX.",
